$ but translated $h$ units right. The vertex of $y=(x-h)^2$ is located at $(h,0)$.\n\n**Watch Out!** It's easy to confuse the translations.\n\n- For $y=(x-3)^2$, we subtract $3$ from $x$ inside the parentheses, and the parabola moves to the right, *not* to the left (even though it seems like it should be the other way around).\n- Likewise, for $y=(x+2)^2$, we add $2$ to $x$ inside the parentheses, and the parabola moves to the left, *not* to the right." 13194139535797 17592186045417 false] [17592186069980 1064 "Adding a value to ![](images/2e/2eb046be7e52e5a72d29a1333f9cf483411f0a8d6d897fe53014cc1952c6f759.svg) will **translate** (shift) the parabola up or down the ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-axis. For instance, adding ![](images/f5/f5f3224583db57b9cfe323c8489ef5e5271000002b5ea253eb98fd067a858b2d.svg) to ![](images/2e/2eb046be7e52e5a72d29a1333f9cf483411f0a8d6d897fe53014cc1952c6f759.svg) will move each point on the parabola ![](images/f5/f5f3224583db57b9cfe323c8489ef5e5271000002b5ea253eb98fd067a858b2d.svg) units up.\n\n![](images/2a/2a233fc5fe21dd3ffd460ab3fa343ac3c4587bca17fd958343309bc723a2cda5.png)\n\nOn the other hand, subtracting ![](images/6c/6cb44f25e489afb06ec62d2e95c4d235ece77eb36e2327b856264d2fb8b22c21.svg) will move each point of the parabola ![](images/6c/6cb44f25e489afb06ec62d2e95c4d235ece77eb36e2327b856264d2fb8b22c21.svg) units down.\n\n![](images/5b/5bcc36e857503b3faf90d1cbb58750150dc7849a0f2a0b3c58b77319ffff1224.png)\n\nIn general, the graph of ![](images/00/00abc9adb93347077819fc66fecc1e7eef09e68fc6f8e94a76e27c8eb70b13a0.svg) looks like the standard parabola ![](images/2e/2eb046be7e52e5a72d29a1333f9cf483411f0a8d6d897fe53014cc1952c6f759.svg) but translated ![](images/8d/8dc6f7e80ecaac9fa07890ce1881dd51de319597ae8b1dce821aa03c1f3eff06.svg) units up. The vertex of ![](images/00/00abc9adb93347077819fc66fecc1e7eef09e68fc6f8e94a76e27c8eb70b13a0.svg) is located at ![](images/e8/e8c4c8598a8228afb25cbf13